#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-SEND-0119 expect=violation domain=CO
#note "NOTE THE GAP: COVAL1 is NOT declared while COVAL2 is. evalColumnSeriesMetadata collects suffix 0 (the `name` COVAL) and suffix 2 (matching name_pattern ^COVAL\\d+$); the run [0..2] needs three members and only two are present, so the gap test hi-lo+1 != size returns TRUE. length= is MANDATORY on every COVAL* column: omitting it declares length 0 and the rule would fire for the wrong reason. M3-D22 moved this rule's Executability from 'Fully Executable' to 'Partially Executable - Possible Underreporting' with no Check change: column_series_metadata reads only DECLARED column lengths and never a data cell, so the sheet's Condition ('Comment value > 200 characters in length') cannot be detected on an unsplit comment. Reading the data would need a length-of-value operator the engine does not have."
#library standard=sendig version=3-1-1
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1
dataset CO label="Comments"
col STUDYID type=Char length=12 label="Study Identifier"
col DOMAIN  type=Char length=2  label="Domain Abbreviation"
col USUBJID type=Char length=20 label="Unique Subject Identifier"
col COSEQ   type=Num  label="Sequence Number"
col COVAL   type=Char length=200 label="Comment"
col COVAL2  type=Char length=200 label="Comment Part 2"
---
S1 | CO | 001 | 1 | First two hundred characters of the comment | continuation text
S1 | CO | 002 | 1 | Another comment | more text
---
